# scripts/pii-patterns.local.example
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TEMPLATE for project-specific PII patterns. Contains ONLY obvious fake
# placeholders — never put real PII in this file (it is committed to the repo).
#
# Usage:
#   cp scripts/pii-patterns.local.example scripts/pii-patterns.local
#   # then edit pii-patterns.local (gitignored) and replace the placeholders
#   # with the real names / companies / paths you want the scanner to flag.
#
# Each non-empty, non-comment line is one regex pattern. They are OR-joined.
# scripts/pii-patterns.local is gitignored — it stays on your machine only.
# For CI, set a repository secret named PII_PATTERNS with the same content
# (see .github/workflows/pii-scan.yml).
<REPLACE_WITH_REAL_NAME_1>
<REPLACE_WITH_REAL_NAME_2>
<REPLACE_WITH_REAL_COMPANY_1>
<REPLACE_WITH_REAL_BUSINESS_FINGERPRINT_1>
/Users/<REPLACE_WITH_USERNAME>/Documents/<REPLACE_WITH_PRIVATE_DIR>
